**Chapter 10-5: The Outcome of the Detour**

—The mental preparation Subaru had made regarding utilizing Reinhard for transportation ended up being useless in two ways.

"…You might find it a bit unsettling, but you should get used to it soon."

The action taken by Reinhard, who prefaced it with those words, was to heft the dragon carriage carrying Subaru and the others—Patlash and all—onto his shoulders and charge fiercely through the sky—no, *dash* through it.

"Ababababababa…!"

The scenery outside the window streamed by at high speed, yet the visual bug of feeling almost no shaking inside the carriage made Subaru shiver violently, clinging to Beatrice.

He more or less understood the principle. In short, it was the same as the 'Wind Protection' blessing possessed by a ground dragon. The problem was that the one demonstrating it was human—Reinhard—and he was running at a speed so nonsensical that questioning common sense felt foolish.

"I've had this done to me once before, you know. Now it's your turn to experience it, Subaru-bro and everyone."
"B-but, can you really get used to this!?"

Meili, who was sitting quietly with her cheek propped on her knee on the seat, exuded the composure of an experienced veteran. Petra timidly clung to Meili's cloak as she asked. "Fuhun," Meili chuckled.
"Petra-chan had things she was scared of too, huh? I'm surprised~"
"Scared? It's more like when something happens outside your imagination, you get shocked, right? He's even more nonsensical than I heard, 'Sword Saint'-sama."
"...Indeed. Even I haven't heard of any previous 'Sword Saints' being this far outside common sense. I suppose it's safe to say Reinhard is special."

After the latter part of the conversation with Meili, seeing Petra direct the water (turning the topic) toward him, Old Man Rom patted his own head as he answered.

Old Man Rom, whose huge frame was crammed uncomfortably into the carriage seat, also didn't seem accustomed to this 'Reinhard Running Method'. For the sake of his mental peace, he had one hand pressed against the wall.

It seemed that within the Felt camp, this method of travel was not adopted on a daily basis. This in itself was an incredible advantage, he thought.

"If we relied on such a method outside of emergencies, his reputation would likely suffer as 'improperly exploiting the Sword Saint'. After all, even the Kingdom would be troubled if the authority of the 'Sword Saint' were to diminish... It could even lead to him being forbidden from using this travel method, not just leaving the country."
"Ah, that joke-like Reinhard Law..."

In response to Old Man Rom's wry remark, Subaru spoke of the otherworldly, nonsensical international law unique to this world.

The Reinhard Law, as the name implied, was a law established with the sole objective of preventing the 'Sword Saint' Reinhard van Astrea from leaving the Kingdom of Lugunica. It sounded like a joke, but when one truly grasped the extent of his abnormality, it was hard to call it an overreaction.

However—

"Yeah, I get that Reinhard's power is crazy, like, almost stupidly so, but I wish people would see that he's not the type to cause trouble in other countries."
"Oh? Despite being in another camp, you hold Reinhard in such high regard?"
"Well, he's my friend. And it'd be sad if he was the only one left behind when we all go on a trip abroad. Like a trip to Vollachia... Nah, there aren't any fun places in Vollachia. Unless Mr. Flop and Miss Medium use their authority to build, like, an amusement park or something."

Somehow, skillfully, by stealing Abel's attention or winning him over, he wished they could somehow squander the empire's finances on entertainment and establish a huge amusement park.

"Garfiel, what are you looking at, I suppose?"
"Nah, I was thinkin' if Big Bro could do somethin' similar, I'd make things way easier for the boss and everyone. But feelin' is 'it's about suitability, it's about the self', I ain't got what it takes to do the same thing as Big Bro, ya know?"

While Subaru envisioned the Vollachia Land construction plan, Garfiel, addressed by Beatrice, ground his teeth and expressed regret in that manner.

Certainly, in terms of raw strength, Garfiel seemed capable of the same feats as Reinhard. But without the 'Wind Protection' blessing, the comfort level would be hellish. Besides, treating a sworn brother like a draft horse, even in an emergency, would weigh on one's conscience.

"Ah, I get why the Reinhard Running Method isn't put into practical use. Yeah, this is a heavy feeling."
『I'm glad you understand. I, too, feel hesitant about this outside of emergencies.』
"You just joined the conversation like it's normal..."

Reinhard, who naturally projected his voice, was using the effect of the 'Telepathy' blessing, which Subaru had experienced once in Priestella.

It seemed this time he was projecting his voice to others besides Subaru, as Petra and the others, who suddenly heard Reinhard's voice in their heads, couldn't hide their surprised expressions. Meili, however, seemed to have resistance to this 'Telepathy' blessing as well, maintaining her smug face.

Anyway—

"For now, the shock of the Reinhard Running Method has settled a bit, but there's still the other impact to process. Is it true? About that... Filol girl's appearance."
『——Yes, it's an indisputable fact.』

Though invisible, Subaru could tell Reinhard had nodded in affirmation. He swallowed the shock of the reported fact once more as a heavy sigh.

It was the astonishing new development that had occurred in the royal capital while Subaru and the others were at the Pleiades Watchtower—the contact from the 'Divine Dragon Church' and the appearance of a person named Filol, who had made the insignia shine.

The fact that this organization, which had kept a low profile until now, had appeared carrying a fact that couldn't be ignored in terms of the Royal Selection, naturally caused intense agitation in Subaru as Emilia's knight, a Royal Selection candidate.

However—

"—The fact that Crusch-sama is saved is the best news."

The seismic shock to the Royal Selection was also an unmissable event, but among the topics brought up, the one with the greatest meaning for Subaru was Crusch's recovery.

Crusch, who in Priestella had fallen prey to the Sin Archbishop of Lust, had been burdened with an incurable curse that caused her constant agony. The self-reproach for being unable to protect Crusch while sharing the same battlefield had remained long and deep within Subaru, like a thorn.

"Honestly, if ripping that curse out of Crusch-sama meant my whole body turned pitch black, I'd have been fine with that."

Crusch, doused in the blood of 'Lust', had suffered unspeakable damage. Subaru, too, had undergone the same baptism of blood, but the resulting damage was vastly different from Crusch's.

Of course, there were effects all over his body, but unlike the continuously suffering Crusch, it was only things like grotesque failed tattoos on his limbs. Even those were completely lost when his arm was blown off, and the effect on his leg was only something to be startled by when remembering it in the bathroom or bath.

Somehow, Subaru's body was able to take on that damage from Crusch in exchange for pain. There had been an option to save Crusch with that, but—

"Crusch-sama... didn't give a strong nod of agreement."

After the resolution in Priestella, she had refused Subaru's offer to take on the curse, saying she couldn't burden him as he headed for the Pleiades Watchtower. Her condition had been a constant worry ever since.

That she was healed was undoubtedly good news for Subaru.

Although—

"It's unbearable that the very parties involved cannot wholeheartedly rejoice in that recovery."

As Old Man Rom's grave words stated, the fact that Crusch's recovery was achieved by the hands of an organization called the 'Divine Dragon Church' meant profound pain for her and her camp.

Subaru understood that much. Precisely because he understood, he couldn't say anything careless. Things like, even if it put them at a significant disadvantage in the Royal Selection, being alive was the most important thing, or such easy words.

"But, that person Filol appearing, and making the Priestess insignia shine... that's not good, right?"
"That's right~. Just when we finally had one Royal Selection candidate drop out, opening a slot, now that slot gets filled and we're back to square one~."
"...Meili-chan, if you don't choose your words carefully, I'll get angry too. We even went to the tower because of that."
"Even though the helmet guy ruined that... Alright, alright, don't get mad~. Yes yes, I was in the wrong~."

Perhaps remembering her role as a little devil, Meili, who had been teasing various things, insincerely apologized to Petra, who was giving her a stern look. Letting out a small sigh at Meili's attitude, Petra said "Anyway," and continued,
"Leaving Meili-chan's sharp tongue aside... 'Not good' isn't just about the slot problem. Because, that Filol person, she has blonde hair and red eyes, right?"
"...Right, that's the point. That means..."
"—That's the characteristic of the Lugunica royal family, right? And also, the name of the princess who was kidnapped fifteen years ago was, if I recall..."
"—Filol."

Putting a finger to her lips, Petra recalled her knowledge. At the end of her words, as a pause for the crucial final word, another person took over.—Old Man Rom.

Old Man Rom became the focus of all eyes in the carriage, but he kept his gaze lowered to the space between his knees.
"The name of the daughter of the king's younger brother who disappeared from the royal castle fifteen years ago was Filol. Precisely the same name as the nun of the 'Divine Dragon Church' who reportedly stormed the castle this time."
"And the story is that nun made the insignia shine in front of many people in the castle. If that story is true, it's understandable that a trouble-shaking the Royal Selection has occurred, I suppose."

Having shared the facts that sent shockwaves through Lugunica's royal castle and the surrounding circumstances, a solemn air spread inside the dragon carriage.

Yet, there, Subaru deliberately prepared to ignore the mood and spoke up. "Hey."
"I'm not quite convinced by that, you know."
『——Convinced? You mean?』
"Part of me is getting used to conversing with a voice in my head, but what everyone's concerned about is that, right? That Filol person from the 'Divine Dragon Church' might be the Lugunica royalty who disappeared fifteen years ago. And the insignia shining is like proof of being royalty?"
"Yeah, that's right. What about that isn't convincing?"
"Well, because... Felt was under the same conditions, wasn't she?"

Unfortunately, even tracing back the memories of that accursed day the Royal Selection began, Subaru hadn't heard Felt's declaration. That was because he messed up big time and got thrown out of the throne room before that.

However, even though he wasn't present, what happened in that place after Subaru's expulsion and what Felt said were properly shared with him later.

And from the start, the issue of the royalty from fifteen years ago had surfaced there as well.

"In other words, the situation is the same as with Felt. Well, personally, I think the scenario where a princess secretly taken out of the castle has been living as a commoner among the people is hot, so I prefer the storyline where Felt is the royalty..."
"Hmm, I see.——But, as you imagine, if Felt were the princess of the Lugunica Kingdom, then the Royal Selection would be decided as Felt's victory. Is that alright with you?"
"Eh?"

At Old Man Rom's pointed remark, made with one eye narrowed, Subaru widened his eyes.

He thought it might be an ill-natured joke, but no correction came. Moreover, everyone besides Subaru seemed to agree with Old Man Rom's view.

Finding himself unexpectedly in the minority—no, as a sole faction—Subaru was shaken.

"N-no, no, no, why?"
"Why, you ask? That's just how it is, ain't it? The whole reason we're doin' the Royal Selection is 'cause the royal family vanished, right? But if that turns out not to be true, then it's only natural for the surviving royal to become king, ain't it?"
"H-h, hereditary succession?"
『I wish you'd choose your words, but yes, that's the case.』

Reprimanded thus by the two martial members, Garfiel and Reinhard, Subaru realized the gap between his perception and that of the otherworlders. He let out an "Ah—" sigh.

For Natsuki Subaru, born and raised in Japan, having a country's representative chosen not by bloodline but by other factors was natural. The very situation of the Royal Selection itself, leaning toward an election system familiar to Subaru, also had an influence.

But rather, for the otherworlders, it was natural for the next king after the current king to be the prince, and if the prince became king, his child would become the next prince.

Therefore, if it were confirmed that Felt was royalty, the natural flow would be for Felt to assume the next throne, and the Royal Selection would lose its very function——

"So that means, if it was confirmed Felt was royalty, it would've been bad!?"
"That's why it stopped at the stage of suspicion, allowing the Royal Selection to proceed. Boy, are you properly serving as that young lady's knight?"
"Stop it! I was just a bit ignorant of common sense! We've got smart young people growing up properly here, like Beako, Petra, and Garfiel!"
"Let me correct you, but the pretty and charming Betty is the most mature one here."

Beatrice, who was being hugged and sitting on his lap, puffed out her chest there. Watching Subaru stroke her head, Old Man Rom looked exasperated and patted his own head.

He saw. Indeed, a slight discrepancy in understanding had led him to make a fool of himself. But even so, Subaru's turn for questions wasn't over.

"Had a little stumble, but my doubt ain't resolved yet. I get that if royalty is confirmed, the Royal Selection loses its meaning. But ultimately, that suspicion about whether Filol-chan-san is the real deal is the same as with Felt, right? So then..."
『——We must determine which one is the true royal.』
"————"

It might have been words spoken while trying to keep emotions out as much as possible. All the more for that, those wordless words from Reinhard felt as sharp as a blade.

Subaru held his breath, letting the meaning of those words sink into his brain.—Determining which one is the real royal, between Felt and Filol.

"It was suspicion without confirmation that allowed the Royal Selection to proceed until today. However, with two potential candidates who might be the missing royalty, we can't possibly leave this be. We must also fear the possibility of someone with malicious intent having infiltrated the Royal Selection."
"Malicious intent... Even if one is royalty, that doesn't automatically make the other one suddenly evil, right? They might just happen to have blonde hair and red eyes..."
"That 'just happening' doesn't occur, which is why it's considered a characteristic unique to the royal family, I suppose."
"But! The insignia shone for both of them, right!?"

Faced with logical explanations from both Old Man Rom and Beatrice, Subaru became emotional. He was in a state where he could only retort emotionally.

To begin with, he couldn't even explain to himself why he was getting so worked up.

If part of the reason for his fondness for Reinhard and Old Man Rom was meeting them right after being summoned, then the same could be said for Felt. He didn't want Felt's way of being and efforts to be denied just because she might not be royalty.

Moreover, he hated the idea of unilaterally vilifying Filol, whom he hadn't even met yet, and accusing her of scheming something.

Above all——

"If they absolutely want royalty to succeed, then when Felt appeared, they could've just ignored the Royal Selection and checked if she was royalty or not with a DNA test or whatever. Instead of doing that, they started the Royal Selection, and Emilia, everyone, how much..."
"Subaru..."

Beatrice, sitting on his lap, looked at Subaru with concern as he bit his lip hard and stifled his voice. Feeling the gentle grasp of her hand, Subaru closed his eyes and took a deep, strong breath. Even so, his heart, struck by intense emotion, thumped wildly and refused to calm down easily.

The Royal Selection was something Emilia, Felt, Crusch, Anastasia, Priscilla—they all faced, staking their beliefs and even their lives on it.

He couldn't accept having the premise twisted just because an unexpected disruption had occurred.

"In that case..."
"In that case, what will you do?"
"Demonstrate with Reinhard, or something, to appeal for the continuation of the Royal Selection..."
『——I see.』
"You 'see' nothing of the sort! Don't say such terrifying things! And you! Don't rashly incite the 'Sword Saint'! What would you do if he seriously carried it out!?"
"If it comes to that, I'll join in too, ya know!"
"Garf-san, things are getting complicated now, so could you be quiet for a bit? Okay?"

In response to Subaru's agonized words from being at an impasse, Old Man Rom and Petra strongly objected. A dynamic and static scolding occurred, and Garfiel, glared at by Petra, wilted with a "Gao...".

But it wasn't all a joke.—No, rather, he was quite serious. With that much resolve, as a knight of a Royal Selection candidate, he had to show his spirit.

"There's a lot to do when we reach the capital...! I feel like I've been moving non-stop for about half a year already..."
"That much is still just the beginning, I suppose. Betty feels like she's been moving non-stop for about eleven and a half years, in fact."
"Don't say such scary things, my head's gonna get messed up..."

In response to Subaru's light remark, Beatrice made an even more powerful quip. Trembling with fear at her words, Subaru sighed at the enormity and multitude of troubles awaiting them in the royal capital.

He was worried about Emilia facing such a situation, and he wanted to visit the reportedly recovered Crusch. He also needed to see the face of that Filol person, and he had to personally confront the traumatizing high-ranking officials about what would happen with the Royal Selection. He wanted to investigate the Al-orb hanging from his neck and the various factors that led to that outrageous act.

But for the immediate present, what needed to be dealt with now was—

『——Subaru, we're arriving.』
"Seriously? Amazing. Sorry for the detour."

His shift in mindset and the report from Reinhard were perfectly timed.

Judging from the scenery streaming by at high speed, it was imaginable, but the travel speed was truly extraordinary. In terms of speed alone, Cecilus might be faster at moving, but unfortunately, he likely lacked the physical strength to carry a dragon carriage, so a 'Cecilus Running Method' seemed unlikely to be established.

Even if someone could carry one person on their back, they might manage something similar—but while he was thinking such things, the scenery outside the window abruptly regained a sense of reality.

The high-speed streaming stopped, and the dragon carriage was slowly lowered to the ground. In other words, arrival at the destination. As if to prove it——

"—Just what is the meaning of this!?"
"————"

Hearing that voice first, Subaru vigorously stood up and, with a startled "Nkyah!" from Beatrice whom he was holding, leaped out of the dragon carriage.

There stood Reinhard, who had run while carrying the dragon carriage without breaking a sweat, and Patlash, who seemed to have been quite tense from being carried by Reinhard.

And then, at the nostalgic gate of the Roswaal manor, standing there with eyes wide at the absurd appearance of the dragon carriage, was someone with blue hair——

"Ugh!"
"Subaru!? Wha-wha-what's wrong, I suppose!?"

Subaru, who had instinctively clutched his chest and dropped to one knee on the spot, caused Beatrice—who had been dragged outside with him—to roll her eyes in panic. While letting a flustered Beatrice pat his head and shoulders, Subaru felt a pang in his chest from the stimulating sight.

Because the one standing in front of Roswaal Manor, welcoming them, was——

"I realize just how precious your familiar appearance is..."
"...No matter when or where we meet, you're always like this, aren't you?"

Saying that, with a face that seemed both exasperated and relieved—a deeply nuanced expression—the one in the maid uniform—yes, in the maid uniform, Rem—let out a sigh.


---


Taking advantage of the speed of the Reinhard Running Method, Subaru had pleaded on the way to the royal capital to make a stop at Roswaal Manor.

The purpose was, needless to say, to have Rem also be present at the occasion to retrieve 'memories' from the Sin Archbishop of 'Gluttony', Roy Alphard—one of the reasons for heading to the royal capital.

"I doubt negotiations with 'Gluttony' will go smoothly, but Al somehow managed to drag that information out of him. So there's no reason I can't do it. Besides, I've already missed the scene of Ram and Rem's reunion. If I were to miss seeing Rem's 'memories' return at this stage, I'd never recover...!"

To Subaru's tearful, passionate appeal, Reinhard agreed without a single hint of displeasure, even though he probably wanted to return to Felt's side even a second sooner.

He really could only be called a great friend. Subaru also wanted to grant any request Reinhard might have, but if he were asked to shoulder a dragon carriage and make a detour of hundreds of kilometers, it was questionable whether he could nod so readily.

But Reinhard had actually done it for him.

Moreover, what Reinhard had undertaken wasn't just that—


"—Sorry for making you accompany me all the way here."
"It's fine, I don't mind. Besides, though I'm not aware of it, I've also been a victim of the Sin Archbishop of 'Gluttony''s authority. It seems I've had at least one friend made to be forgotten."
"Yeah... Come to think of it, that guy, after being resigned to being forgotten, apparently said it was a good chance to challenge you, Reinhard. Something about you not knowing his hand now, so he could win..."
"That's... honestly, something to look forward to."

Glancing sideways at Reinhard, who raised his brows slightly and then smiled with genuine delight, Subaru internally apologized to Julius for possibly saying something unnecessary and stirring things up.

He might have crushed a possible chance for victory. But considering Julius, who believed keeping his hand known only to himself was unfair, he might actively show his cards. So, apologizing outwardly was on hold.

—And so on. He indulged in such inconsequential thoughts because it was a place with such heavy air.

"...As expected of the Prison Tower."
A strangely cold sweat trickled down Subaru's murmuring forehead.

He wasn't particularly flustered, nor had he been running. Yet the cold sweat that emerged and flowed was his entire body's rejection reaction to this space.

The stone spire built near the royal castle on the uppermost level of the royal capital, Lugunica, served as a prison housing some of the kingdom's most serious criminals. Naturally, to prevent easy meetings with any prisoner, each solitary cell was sealed tight with iron doors.

Unlike the style common in manga where prisoners are behind iron bars, Subaru, stepping inside, felt a mix of relief and disappointment in a seven-to-three ratio.

"Sure, among the guys on the Sword Wolf Island, there were some who were proper criminals, but they were more like straightforward villains..."
It felt odd to call it a national trait, but the crimes committed by his comrades on Sword Wolf Island Ginusnave—Hearin, Veitz, Idra—were basically of the rampage-type, without insidiousness. Though sometimes, like with Hearin, there were merciless reasons for being thrown in, like falling into slavery, even those considered serious criminals only differed in the scale of their rampages—small or large.

On the other hand, the atmosphere of this Prison Tower, which housed Lugunica's serious criminals, felt utterly different to Subaru, who knew the Sword Wolf Island; it had a blood-soaked stench of a completely different nature.

"So, is the rate of Witch Cultists being caught here really high?"
"That's right. Considering they are mainly active in Lugunica, that thinking is correct. In fact, 'Wrath' is also imprisoned in the basement here."
"Basement... So they're keeping distance from 'Gluttony'."
"Taking every precaution. While their captive situations differ, we can't let people near 'Wrath' carelessly. Not even the other prisoners."

The authority of the Sin Archbishop of 'Wrath', Sirius Romanée-Conti, was something like mental contamination, swallowed by her words or atmosphere, spreading like airborne infection. Considering its influence, even with her movements sealed, one could hardly say the danger was completely removed.

In fact, it seemed some of the unpleasant miasma drifting through this Prison Tower might be emanating from that Sin Archbishop of 'Wrath'.

"I feel a physical revulsion, but we might have to talk to her eventually too."
"When that time comes, let me know. I'll attend as well, like this time."
"That's reassuring. I'm seriously counting on you."

The dependability of Reinhard, who pounded his chest and took on the task. However, Sirius's authority was one where Reinhard's strength could potentially backfire. Caution was needed.

In any case, the reason Subaru and the others visited the Prison Tower today wasn't for her. Sorry, but for now, Sirius would have to savor the cold air of the basement.

Instead—

"—This way."

The one who indicated a single door, saying that, was the Prison Tower guard leading them. With a face evenly split between strong tension and professional awareness, Subaru nodded to him and looked at the door.

A door that felt cold and oppressive just by looking at it.—Beyond that door was imprisoned the Sin Archbishop of 'Gluttony'.

"Though, given it's probably a state similar to the Al-orb, whether the person themselves is conscious is questionable."

Based on his own experience, when sealed inside a black sphere, it was an indescribable sensation, like being immersed in lukewarm water unable to move.

In an environment where even consciousness couldn't be maintained clearly, he wanted to award Beatrice the "Iyarī Subaru Award" for her hard work and dedication in unraveling the forbidden magic mechanism for Subaru's sake. But with nominees alone filling both hands, he needed to deliberate carefully.

"Subaru? Why are you squeezing Betty's cheek, I suppose?"
"Ah, since the Iyarī Subaru Award can't be given immediately, I'm substituting with an expression of affection instead..."
"You can do as you like once our business is done, so focus on what's in front of us now."

Perhaps seeing through his touch-seeking from nervousness, Beatrice scolded him seriously. Pouting slightly, Subaru let out a breath and said, "Right."

Beatrice at the front gate, Reinhard at the rear gate—this was the best formation Subaru had assembled for visiting 'Gluttony' in the Prison Tower. Ideally, he wanted the concerned party, Rem, to be present, but he didn't expect things to go well on the very first attempt at discussion anyway.

Persuading or coercing 'Gluttony' was anticipated to require patient, repeated attempts.

"Anyway, since he's sealed with Yin Magic, Beako is essential for releasing it."
"Leave it to Betty, I suppose. And if the opponent tries to rampage immediately upon release, 'Sword Saint', you will beat him down, I suppose."
"Yes, understood. I won't let him lay a finger on either of you. Rest assured."
"Honestly, that's super reassuring. So then..."

Relying on the power of his overly dependable allies, Subaru signaled to the guard to unlock the door. As the guard slowly pushed the door open, Subaru clenched his fists tightly.

—In the dimly lit tower, especially in the dark depths of the solitary cell, Roy Alphard was imprisoned, solidified by Yin Magic into a monolith-like form. The plan was to awaken that Roy, to make him disgorge Rem's 'memories', the 'Names' and 'memories' of all victims.

Conversing with the Sin Archbishops would be a battle that eroded one's own sanity, but if there was a definite reward beyond that, Subaru was determined to stubbornly pursue it—


"—Huh?"

Subaru, who had been holding his breath for that resolve, unintentionally let it out.

As his eyes adjusted to the gloom, the scene within the cell was not what Subaru had anticipated. He expected to see Roy Alphard embedded in a black slate-like monolith, in a specimen-like state.

However, what lay there was a completely unexpected sight.

"————"

Subaru froze, not understanding. But a hand softly pushed him aside on the shoulder, and Reinhard stepped into the cell instead. Right beside him, Beatrice leaned her whole body against Subaru—no, she was supporting him.

Because the strength had left Subaru's legs, and he was on the verge of collapsing.

With the nearly collapsing Subaru and Beatrice supporting him behind, Reinhard, who had advanced into the depths of the cell, looked at *that* scattered on the cold prison floor and shook his head.

Then he turned around and spoke.

"—Unfortunately, he's dead."

At Reinhard's feet, the gruesome corpse of the Sin Archbishop of 'Gluttony'—'Bizarre Eating' Roy Alphard—lay scattered and rolled about, limbs torn apart, body in pieces, presenting a scene of utter carnage. That was what lay there.
